                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_404">Norwich, Norfolk.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>Pressmark 'C. x'
                        at beginning and end (fols. 3r, 114v).</p><p>Quire xi of the old numeration
                        is missing: it presumably contained the text 'De combustione ecclesie
                        cathedralis sancte trinitatis norwic'' recorded in the old table of
                        contents, but now missing.</p><p>The dialect of the English pieces is East
                        Anglian (see Joseph Hall, Early Middle English, p. 591).</p><p>Bale saw De
                        combustione . . . at Norwich, or knew of it (Index, p. 517).</p><q type="pressmark">C. x</q></provenance>
